# AutoBonk

Read `PROJECT.md` once, then `rules/ta_rules.md`, `charts/pm_levels_index.md`, and the live book `alerts/levels.yaml`. Read `AGENTS.md` for what an agent may do.

- Ideas come from operator charts in `charts/`. Do not use TradeWhisperer, GEX, or fundamentals.
- Discord forwards are empty unless read with `scripts/discord_ta.py`. Run `ingest` so images are local files.
- Draft plans for the Agentic account only. Do not trade the taxable account or the IRA.
- The checker sends a qualifying Agentic entry, and the sell when that contract is still open. Any other order waits until the operator replies confirm.
- Monday 2026-10-19 through Wednesday 2026-10-21 are paper. Those checker rows stay in `alerts/paper.md`. The candle, RSI, SMAs, nearby levels, and volume for a row are in `alerts/context.md`. Do not place an order for a paper session, including after confirm. A paper row does not fill the journal Trade column and is not a pattern.
- Thursday 2026-10-22 is the first live session. Agentic only. One contract. The live debit has to fit the Agentic account balance, read on that check. A checker entry is a plan in `alerts/live.md`. The checker sends that contract when the far target can still reach the strike and the debit fits. Halfway refuses 0DTE only. A balance that cannot be read, a cash strike of none, an empty ladder, or a debit the balance cannot pay stays a plan, and no order is sent. The exit of an open Agentic contract is a sell. A sell that is already working is not sent again.
- The fade test in `alerts/fade_forward.md` covered 2026-10-19 through 2026-10-21. The gate passed: profit factor 3.17, net +8.56 stock points, 13 closes. The fade record is paper. The live checker stays on the retest.
- Do not edit `config/agentic.yaml` or `.env`. Do not print `TA_BOT_TOKEN` or account numbers.
- Do not invent TA rules. If `rules/ta_rules.md` is still the blank template, stop and ask.
- While `config/freeze.yaml` is active, no change may move a replayed decision (`scripts/tests/test_freeze.py`). Rule ideas become proposals in `learning/proposals/` (see `learning/proposals.md`). Never write the checker's tapes in `alerts/`. Only the checker writes them.
- After new TA or a confirmed trade, update `learning/journal.md`. Patterns come only from trades that were taken.
- The fast RSI line is purple: 14 RSI. Yellow is the 14 SMA smoothing. A claim or lose is a finished 10-minute close beyond the level by half the 14-period ATR. A close inside that band has not broken the level. The 15-cent touch is still only the wick. An alert is not an order.
- Buy calls on a red candle and puts on a green candle. Sell calls into strength and puts into weakness. Posted levels are targets, so profit can be taken before the print.
- Before an intraday entry, read `learning/training.md`. Finished 10-minute bars are the only candles visible. A confirmed drill is an observation, not an order.
- Play the levels in the operator's note, including price close to a level. RSI is confluence, not a blocker. Do not skip a level because every confluence does not line up.
- Every support can flip to resistance, and every resistance can flip to support. The flip is a finished 10-minute close beyond the level by half the 14-period ATR. A close inside that band has not flipped the level. A later close back through flips it again. The flipped side targets the posted numbers in that direction.
- 4h and daily RSI choose which levels are likely in play. They do not have to agree with the 10-minute play. Undecided RSI means the 10-minute RSI drives, especially price at RSI 50.
- The first target in a note is the next number. "Possibly" is a further target if that one is also lost or claimed. Hitting the first target does not close the trade. Trimming or rolling up the chain is optional.
- Skip a lower level when the next number has been tagged and the close came back through it. A later close through that number clears the skip. The 2026-10-19 AAPL call at 345.18 is the example: 345.40 was tagged and did not hold. Skip an entry when the priced contract is none. A check more than 20 minutes late still writes that session's paper row, or the live plan on a live session, and does not send the Discord alert. A prior session does not gain a new entry. After a reclaim stop at a level, skip the next entry there (reason `fresh`) until a finished 10-minute bar has traded one 14-period ATR away from that level on either side. The level's next retest after that is fresh. The memory resets each session.
- A live long option is one contract, and the debit has to fit the account balance. Look first at 0DTE or the next expiration, at the money or in the money. A reasonable out-of-the-money contract is allowed when theta and the distance to the posted target still leave room for it to gain. Do not take 0DTE in the last hour before the 13:00 PT cash close. Do not take a 0DTE strike past the halfway point between the stock and the far target. The exit clock is that contract's broker sellout when the instrument has one. Robinhood's late-close list runs to 12:45 PT. An index is out at 1:00 PM PT. Any other equity option is out at 12:30 PT. If the sellout and that list cannot be read, keep 12:45 PT for an equity option and 1:00 PM PT for an index. An entry still open after its cutoff is closed on a later check. A contract with no expiration still leaves on the 12:50 bar. That close is the reclaim, the last target, or that cutoff, and it does not send the Discord alert. Do not sell before that cutoff. Do not cut it unless the level is invalidated or theta will hurt the contract significantly.
